# 本地配置文件（包含敏感信息）
# ===================
backend/config.yaml
deploy/config.yaml
backend/.installed
# Key material and local operator config, repo-wide. These were briefly scoped to
# `scripts/**` only, which was the wrong shape twice over: the repo had NO global
# key patterns at all (a stray `ops/deploy.key` or `backend/tls.pem` was
# committable), and scoping them implied `scripts/` was special when the risk is
# everywhere. Extension- and filename-based on purpose: a `*secret*` /
# `*credential*` substring glob would shadow ~48 legitimate tracked sources
# (`security_secret.go`, `credentials_redact.go`, `credential_shadow.go`, …),
# recreating the tracked-but-ignored trap that `scripts/checks/gitignore-script-homes.py`
# exists to prevent. Name a real secret file after its content, not its extension,
# and it is on you — that is what review is for.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
config.local.*
scripts/config.*

# ===================
# 其他
# ===================
# TK override: upstream's bare `tests` matched any directory named `tests` at any
# depth, then took two negations to hand `deploy/tests/` back. It ignored nothing
# real (this repo's suites live in `__tests__/`, `frontend/e2e/` and Go `_test.go`)
# while standing ready to swallow a future `frontend/tests/` or `ops/tests/`.
# Upstream merges will conflict here; resolve toward tracking test directories.
# TK override: upstream ignores `CLAUDE.md` outright; TokenKey tracks it as the
# project agent contract. The upstream rule's un-rooted reach (matching at any
# depth) protected nothing here — the only other CLAUDE.md in the tree is inside
# the `dev-rules` submodule, which this file does not govern — so the rule is
# dropped rather than narrowed-then-undone.
# Upstream merges will conflict here; resolve toward tracking it.
# `.claude/` is agent state, so it stays ignore-by-default: the three tracked
# entries are named back explicitly and everything else (worktrees, history,
# todos, mcp.local.json, tmp renders) is ignored without needing to be listed.
# This is the one place the split earns its keep — most of the directory really
# is untracked local state.
.claude/*
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/skills
# TK override: upstream ignores a bare `scripts`, which (being pattern-less) matched
# every `scripts/` directory at any depth. TokenKey keeps load-bearing tooling there
# (223 tracked files: preflight gates, sentinels, ops) — all force-added past this
# rule, so a NEW checker or skill script was silently dropped from commits. Like
# `docs/` above, the rule ignored nothing real: the only untracked files under
# `scripts/` are 62 `.pyc` already covered by the `__pycache__/` rule below. So the
# ignore is dropped rather than re-included five times over.
# Upstream merges will conflict here; resolve toward tracking these.
.code-review-state
#openspec/
code-reviews/
# TK override: same as `CLAUDE.md` above — the root `AGENTS.md` carries the
# sync.sh-managed Codex/Antigravity block and is tracked, and the un-rooted reach
# protected nothing (no other AGENTS.md exists outside the dev-rules submodule).
# Upstream merges will conflict here; resolve toward tracking it.
backend/cmd/server/server
deploy/docker-compose.override.yml
.gocache/
vite.config.js
# TK override: upstream ignores `docs/*` and allowlists a handful of files back,
# because upstream keeps almost no docs in git. TokenKey's policy is the opposite:
# all 104 docs are tracked and load-bearing (every `docs/approved/*` contract,
# `docs/global/*`, the operator runbooks), several enforced by
# `scripts/checks/approved-docs-index.py`. Inverting an ignore for an entire
# directory we fully track is pure complexity: the rule protected zero files while
# needing 14 negations to undo itself, 4 of which named files that never existed
# (`ASYNC_IMAGE_TASKS.md`, `BATCH_IMAGE_MVP.md`, `COMPOSITE_GROUPS.md`,
# `channel-monitor-v2-safe-defaults.md`) — nobody could tell, because the block's
# net effect was nothing. So `docs/` is now a normal tracked directory: a new doc
# is committable and a stray note shows up in `git status` instead of vanishing.
# Scratch that should never be committed goes in `docs/_scratch/`.
# Upstream merges will conflict in this region; resolve toward this shape.
docs/_scratch/
.serena/
.codex/
frontend/coverage/
aicodex
output/
.codegraph/

# Vitest / Vite cache at repo root
.vite/

